Define batch-results as a series of number.

Pull a rabbit.
    Have rabbit start a task as batch-1: return 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5. Done.
    Have rabbit start a task as batch-2: return 6 + 7 + 8 + 9 + 10. Done.
    Have rabbit start a task as batch-3: return 11 + 12 + 13 + 14 + 15. Done.
    Insert (the awaited result of batch-1) into batch-results.
    Insert (the awaited result of batch-2) into batch-results.
    Insert (the awaited result of batch-3) into batch-results.
Done.

Define grand-total as 0.
For each s in batch-results, repeat: increment grand-total by s. Done.
State "Grand total (1..15): {grand-total converted to text}".

Bind void to run-report, given (the series of number sums):
    Bind void to emit-sums, for each s in sums, output s.

    Bind void to keep-large: for each s from input: if s is greater than 20, output s. Done. Done.

    Bind void to print-labelled: for each s from input: state "Large batch sum: {s converted to text}". Done. Done.

    emit-sums | keep-large | print-labelled.
Done.

Cast run-report on (batch-results).
